==English==

===Etymology===
From {{term|methyl|me(thyl)}} + {{term|thio-}} + (euphonic) ''-n-'' {{suffix||ine}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/mɪˈθʌɪəniːn/|/mɪˈθʌɪənɪn/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# {{amino acid}} A [[sulphur]]-[[containing]] [[essential amino acid]], C<sub>5</sub>H<sub>11</sub>NO<sub>2</sub>S, found in most [[protein]]; it is [[lipotropic]].
#* '''1999''', {{w|Matt Ridley}}, ''Genome'', Harper Perennial 2004, p. 253:
#*: The purpose was to make soya beans more healthy for those for whom they are a staple food by correcting soya beans' natural deficiency in a chemical called '''methionine'''.

====Synonyms====
* [[Met]]

